From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/iavf: fix admin queue read with no interrupt callback

Commit 12e8844f0bda ("net/iavf: check interrupt registration failure")
reads the admin queue in the device alarm when
rte_intr_callback_register() fails. FreeBSD needs that: nic_uio has no
interrupts. Windows needs it too: rte_intr_callback_register() returns
-ENOTSUP there.

Commit 388f0b348065 ("net/iavf: reuse device alarm for PHC sync") arms
the device alarm in all cases, but the alarm reads the admin queue only
when the PF does not give WB_ON_ITR. iavf_dev_init() sets
aq_intr_enabled in all cases, so a command does not poll the admin queue:
it waits for the interrupt thread to read the answer of the PF. When the
PF gives WB_ON_ITR, as the Linux ice driver does, and the callback
registration fails, nothing reads the admin queue. Each command after
aq_intr_enabled is set then waits for its full timeout and fails with
"No response for cmd", iavf_dev_init() fails, and the VF cannot be used.

Keep a flag for a registered callback, and read the admin queue in the
alarm when no callback is registered. When the registration succeeds,
nothing changes.

Tested on Windows 11 with MinGW GCC 16.2 and an E810 VF (8086:1889) on
NetUIO, with the Linux in-tree ice driver on the host: the probe, the
queue setup and the start pass, and testpmd forwards.

Fixes: 388f0b348065 ("net/iavf: reuse device alarm for PHC sync")
Cc: stable@dpdk.org

Signed-off-by: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf.h        | 1 +
 drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c | 9 ++++++---
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf.h b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf.h
index 293adaf6c9..0f04c976b1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf.h
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf.h
@@ -245,6 +245,7 @@ struct iavf_info {
 	int cmd_retval; /* return value of the cmd response from PF */
 	uint8_t aq_resp[IAVF_AQ_BUF_SZ]; /* buffer to store the adminq response from PF */
 	bool aq_intr_enabled;
+	bool aq_intr_cb; /* an interrupt callback reads the admin queue */
 
 	/** iAVF watchdog enable */
 	bool watchdog_enabled;
diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
index 8b8e371435..d800a3382a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
@@ -2887,7 +2887,8 @@ iavf_dev_alarm_handler(void *param)
 	struct iavf_hw *hw = IAVF_DEV_PRIVATE_TO_HW(dev->data->dev_private);
 	uint32_t icr0;
 
-	if (!(vf->vf_res->vf_cap_flags & VIRTCHNL_VF_OFFLOAD_WB_ON_ITR)) {
+	/* Read the admin queue unless an interrupt callback does it. */
+	if (!vf->aq_intr_cb) {
 		iavf_disable_irq0(hw);
 
 		/* read out interrupt causes */
@@ -3074,13 +3075,15 @@ iavf_dev_init(struct rte_eth_dev *eth_dev)
 			&eth_dev->data->mac_addrs[0]);
 
 
+	vf->aq_intr_cb = false;
 	if (vf->vf_res->vf_cap_flags & VIRTCHNL_VF_OFFLOAD_WB_ON_ITR &&
 			/* register callback func to eal lib */
 			rte_intr_callback_register(pci_dev->intr_handle,
-				   iavf_dev_interrupt_handler, (void *)eth_dev) == 0)
-
+				   iavf_dev_interrupt_handler, (void *)eth_dev) == 0) {
+		vf->aq_intr_cb = true;
 		/* enable uio intr after callback register */
 		rte_intr_enable(pci_dev->intr_handle);
+	}
 
 	rte_eal_alarm_set(IAVF_ALARM_INTERVAL,
 			  iavf_dev_alarm_handler, eth_dev);
-- 
